DEFECT-CLASS HUNT (constitution)
 1. SPLIT CLASSIFICATION — the "is this row superseded" decision lives in exactly
    ONE place. cmd: grep -rn "isSupersededPending\|dropSupersededPending" --include=*.go .
    -> isSupersededPending has ONE caller (dropSupersededPending, superseded_pending.go:83);
       dropSupersededPending has ONE caller (loader.go:377, inside LoadDataContext).
    cmd: grep -rn "supersede\|Supersede" --include=*.go internal/ | grep -v superseded_pending | grep -v _test
    -> no parallel implementation anywhere (remaining hits are unrelated prose in
       transaction_pins.go, whatif/handlers.go, retirement tax comments, plus the
       files.go wording).
    I ENUMERATED the consumers rather than trusting the diff:
    cmd: grep -rn "loadCSVFileForAccount\|loadCSVFile(\|ParseCSV(" --include=*.go .
    -> outside dataloader's own tests, the ONLY production caller of the parser is
       loader.go:336 inside LoadDataContext. No surface parses CSVs on its own.
    cmd: per-package tally of `LoadDataContext(|.LoadData()` vs
         `NewTransactionSet(|ParseCSV(` over dashboard, insights, explorer,
         transfers, duplicates, majorexpenses, mcpsvc/{spend,ledger,curate,admin}
    -> every one sources its data from the loader; the only three
       NewTransactionSet( call sites in consumers (explorer/handlers.go:94,
       dashboard/handlers.go:690, mcpsvc/spend/search.go:74) re-wrap an
       ALREADY-LOADED, filtered slice — none re-parses. So every surface reads the
       post-drop set by construction.
    Surface-level confirmation from the oracle on frozen real data:
      search_transactions (all_total 1606, aug/mar/nov/dec/mar windows),
      list_duplicates (dup_unresolved 0), get_transfers (2 windows),
      get_accounts (all three balances), list_major_expenses (5 expenses +
      delivery, totals and counts), list_exceptions (unmatched rows), and
      list_data_files raw counts STAYING raw (files_raw_rows 2837 vs all_total
      1606) — 37/37.
 2. ORDER-OF-STAGES — on master (86d3a7c extraction, loader.go:349-366) NOTHING
    ran between assignStableIDs and deduplicateTransactions except
    setStableIndex; the branch inserts only the drop + buildStableIDIndex there.
    No other stage now sees a shorter slice.
    stableIDIndex publication on EVERY exit path: cmd: grep -n "setStableIndex"
    on both trees -> 3 call sites on each. The two early-exit paths (no CSV files,
    loader.go:293; zero rows parsed, :357) still publish nil exactly as on master;
    only the main path changed (:380, built from SURVIVORS). No path leaves the
    index stale.
    setUnassignedCount is computed at loader.go:420, i.e. AFTER the drop, from the
    final slice (and unassigned rows are never dropped, so the figure is
    unchanged either way).
 3. ZERO-DATE COVERAGE POISONING — probed, not reasoned.
    cmd: go test -count=1 -v -run TestCheckerProbe_ZeroDateSurvival ./internal/services/dataloader/
    (a) an UNPARSEABLE date string -> the row is SKIPPED by the parser
        (loader.go:525-528 `continue`): 2 input rows -> 1 parsed row. No zero Date
        can reach coverage this way.
    (b) a record SHORTER than the Date column index -> the guard
        `idx < len(record)` (loader.go:522) is skipped and the row IS kept with a
        zero Date: probe logged desc="Row C" dateZero=true.
    (c) coverageOf over that mixed slice -> min=2026-01-09 max=2026-01-09, i.e.
        the zero-date row is IGNORED, because coverageOf uses IsZero() as its
        "unset" sentinel. Coverage is NOT poisoned. (An all-zero-date file gets
        min=max=zero, which can neither supersede — zero is never After a real
        maxDate — nor be superseded — a zero Date is never >= a real minDate.)
 4. DISABLED FILES — proved, not assumed.
    Probe TestCheckerProbe_DisabledFileNoCoverage: SetEnabledFiles keeps only the
    OLDER file; the superseding newer file is skipped at loader.go:329-331 BEFORE
    coverage is recorded at :350.
    cmd: go test -count=1 -v -run TestCheckerProbe_DisabledFileNoCoverage ./internal/services/dataloader/
    -> PASS, "loaded with newer file disabled: [Coffee Shop]" — the pending row
       survives, as it must.
    MUTATION PROOF of that probe (disabled files made to contribute coverage) ->
    "--- FAIL: Coffee Shop dropped although the superseding file is DISABLED".

